# examples/spec/raft.cml: Raft leader election as an abstract model.
# The safety property is Election Safety: at most one leader is elected
# per term.  Election Safety is a per-term guarantee, so one term
# suffices to state it and to show its violation; the model is the
# vote-and-win core for a single term.
#
# Reference: Diego Ongaro's raft.tla (the canonical TLA+ specification),
#   https://github.com/ongardie/raft.tla
# Election Safety there:
#   \A i, j : state[i] = Leader /\ state[j] = Leader
#             /\ currentTerm[i] = currentTerm[j] => i = j
# In raft.tla a candidate accumulates votesGranted (the set of servers
# that voted for it) and BecomeLeader fires on a quorum.  Each server
# grants at most one vote per term (RequestVote), so a server appears in
# at most one candidate's votesGranted, and two candidates cannot both
# reach a quorum in the same term.
#
# Here, kept small: 3 servers (0 .. S-1), a quorum of 2.  votes[c]
# accumulates the number of distinct servers that have granted candidate
# c, and used[s] records that server s has already spent its one vote.
# Because two quorums of 3 servers overlap, with each server voting once
# at most one candidate can reach a quorum -- Election Safety.
#
#   cmc --spec examples/spec/raft.cml
#   cmc --spec examples/spec/raft.cml --define BUG   (unsafe: revote)

module raft

const S = 3                     # servers and candidates 0 .. S-1
const Q = 2                     # a quorum majority of S

# used[s] = 1 once server s has granted its single vote for the term
var used : [0 .. S-1 -> 0 .. 1]
# votes[c] = how many distinct servers have granted candidate c
var votes : [0 .. S-1 -> 0 .. S]

init used == [s in 0 .. S-1 -> 0]
init votes == [c in 0 .. S-1 -> 0]

# a server grants its one vote to candidate c: it must not have voted
# yet (RequestVote grants at most one vote per term).  The grant is
# recorded by spending the server's vote and incrementing c's tally.
action grant(s in 0 .. S-1, c in 0 .. S-1):
  when used[s] == 0
  used' = [used except [s] = 1]
  votes' = [votes except [c] = votes[c] + 1]

# the planted bug: a server grants a vote without spending its single
# vote, so one server can grant two candidates -- two candidates can
# then each reach a quorum and both win in one term.
action grant_bug(s in 0 .. S-1, c in 0 .. S-1) [BUG]:
  when votes[c] < S
  votes' = [votes except [c] = votes[c] + 1]

# Election Safety: at most one candidate reaches a quorum in the term,
# so at most one leader is elected.
invariant election_safety: (count c in 0 .. S-1 : votes[c] >= Q) <= 1
